  "what_a_user_may_rely_on": "The per-cell unsupported mask, not only the aggregate. Every repeat agreed on every cell -- Jaccard 1.0, no cell changed its verdict -- so the answer to 'which parts of my mesh are unsupported' is reproducible on this input even though the reconstruction it is computed from is not.",
  "whether_that_is_benign": "Yes, and by a measured margin rather than by luck. Around 556 vertices per repeat sit within 10% of the cut, which is where a sharp threshold on a continuous quantity is vulnerable, and none of them crossed: the largest distance any vertex moved between repeats is 6.44e-06 m against a 0.05 m cut, four orders of magnitude smaller than the band it would have to traverse. The condition to re-check on another scan is that ratio, not this verdict.",
  "what_this_does_not_establish": "Nothing about the cause inside Poisson, which #1024 covers, and nothing about whether the crop rule is the right rule. The figures are not comparable to the record's published values: this harness mirrors the reconstruct-and-crop stage rather than running the full six-stage workflow, and its fused cloud is its own.",
